sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-30> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The 2-state 3-color Turing machine numbered 596,440, which yields complicated behavior from a blank tape, is likely universal, and if so would by most measures be the simplest universal Turing machine.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A complex 2-state 3-color Turing machine is likely the simplest universal one";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Universality in Turing Machines and Other Systems” (from p. 706), p. 709. Scope: 2-state 3-color Turing machines"
}
